 "issue": 1656,
 "issue_title": "Bug: validate pipeline steps container before iteration",
 "issue_body": "## Summary\n`pipeline()` does not validate the `steps` container before iterating. Passing a bare string, a single step tuple, `None`, or a dict produces confusing errors instead of a clear message that `steps` must be a list of step tuples.\n\n## Why it matters\nPipelines are a core user-facing API. A common mistake is to pass `(\"drop_nulls\",)` instead of `[(\"drop_nulls\",)]`. The current error points at the inner string characters or raw iteration behavior, which makes beginner contributor/user debugging harder.\n\n## Evidence\n- `arnio/pipeline.py`: `pipeline()` calls `_validate_pipeline_steps(steps, ...)` without validating that `steps` itself is a list/sequence of step tuples.\n- `_validate_pipeline_steps()` immediately iterates over `steps`, so strings are treated as character sequences and a single tuple is treated as a sequence of strings.\n- Runtime behavior on current source:\n\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\nimport arnio as ar\n\nframe = ar.from_pandas(pd.DataFrame({\"a\": [1]}))\nar.pipeline(frame, \"drop_nulls\")\n# ValueError: Invalid step format: 'd'. Expected (name,) or (name, kwargs)\n\nar.pipeline(frame, (\"drop_nulls\",))\n# ValueError: Invalid step format: 'drop_nulls'. Expected (name,) or (name, kwargs)\n\nar.pipeline(frame, None)\n# TypeError: 'NoneType' object is not iterable\n```\n\n## Reproduction or trigger\n1. Create any `ArFrame`.\n2. Call `ar.pipeline(frame, \"drop_nulls\")`, `ar.pipeline(frame, (\"drop_nulls\",))`, or `ar.pipeline(frame, None)`.\n3. Observe the confusing container-level errors.\n\n## Expected behavior\n`pipeline()` should reject invalid `steps` containers with a clear error such as:\n\n```text\nsteps must be a list of step tuples, for example [(\"drop_nulls\",)]\n```\n\n## Actual behavior\nThe function iterates the invalid object and reports errors about individual characters/items, or leaks a raw `NoneType` iteration error.\n\n## Suggested direction\nAdd an explicit validation branch before `_validate_pipeline_steps()`:\n\n- reject strings/bytes with a targeted `TypeError`\n- reject `None`\n- reject a bare step tuple and suggest wrapping it in a list\n- keep accepting the documented `list[tuple]` shape\n\nAdd tests for each invalid input shape.\n\n## References\n- `arnio/pipeline.py`\n- `tests/test_pipeline.py`\r\n",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/im-anishraj/arnio/issues/1656",
 "pr": 2248,
 "pr_title": "Fix/pipeline step container validation 1656",
 "pr_body": "Closes #1656 \r\n\r\n## Summary\r\nValidate the `steps` container in `pipeline()` before `_validate_pipeline_steps()` iterates it.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n- Reject `None`, `str`, `bytes`, `dict`, and bare step tuples such as `(\"drop_nulls\",)`.\r\n- Bare tuple errors suggest the correct list form, e.g. `[(\"drop_nulls\",)]`.\r\n- Preserve existing valid `list[tuple]` step forms.\r\n- Add regression tests in `tests/test_pipeline.py`.\r\n\r\n## Test plan\r\n- [x] `pytest tests/test_pipeline.py -v -k StepContainer`\r\n- [x] `pytest tests/test_pipeline.py -v`\r\n- [x] `make lint`",
 "fix_commit": "13c3c0890c1c5801851f1291feec7d9c8fca4381",
